{"title":"How plants make food using sunlight","key_idea":"Plants use sunlight, water, and air to make their own food through a process called photosynthesis.","method":["Identify the three things a plant needs: sunlight from the sun, water from the soil through roots, and carbon dioxide gas from the air through tiny holes in leaves.","Understand that these three ingredients are mixed together inside the green parts of the leaf.","Remember that the green colour in leaves comes from chlorophyll, which traps sunlight energy.","Know that plants use this energy to change water and air into sugar, which is food the plant uses to grow."],"worked_example":{"problem":"A plant sits on a sunny windowsill with water in its pot. Explain how it makes food.","steps":["The roots drink water from the soil in the pot.","The leaves take in carbon dioxide from the air through tiny holes called stomata.","Sunlight shines on the green leaves and gives energy.","Inside the leaf, chlorophyll uses all three ingredients to make sugar food for the plant.","The plant uses this sugar to grow bigger and stronger."],"answer":"The plant makes food by combining water, air, and sunlight energy all together."},"key_terms":[{"term":"Photosynthesis","meaning":"the process where plants make their own food using sunlight"},{"term":"Chlorophyll","meaning":"the green substance in leaves that catches sunlight"},{"term":"Stomata","meaning":"tiny holes in leaves that let air in and out"}],"common_mistakes":["Thinking plants eat food like animals do, instead of making it themselves.","Forgetting that plants need air as well as water and sunlight."],"remember":"Sun plus water plus air makes food inside the green leaf.","quick_check":[{"q":"Why do you think a plant kept in a dark room cannot make food?","a":"Because it has no sunlight energy, and photosynthesis needs sunlight to work."},{"q":"If a plant's roots are dry and have no water, what will happen to its ability to make food?","a":"It cannot make food because water is one of the three things needed for photosynthesis."}],"tell_your_child":"Tell your child to think of a plant like a little food factory with three delivery trucks bringing sunlight, water, and air—all three must arrive or the factory stops working. Ask them to point to the green parts of a real plant leaf and explain why those parts are the kitchen where food gets made."}
